  "projects": {
    "2016": [
      {
        "title": "Proposal for GSoC 2016 - Andrea Torlaschi",
        "short_description": "I'm Andrea Torlaschi from Italy.\nI've a Bachelor's degree and now i'm studying for a master's degree in \"Computer Science and Multimedia\" at the...",
        "description": "<p>I'm <strong>Andrea Torlaschi</strong> from Italy.<br>\nI've a Bachelor's degree and now i'm studying for a master's degree in \"Computer Science and Multimedia\" at the University of Pavia.<br>\nOn GitHub i’m “<strong>runnerway</strong>”.</p>\n<p>I would like to spend this summer by coding for OpenKeychain project as a GSoC work.<br>\nSince the first day when the list of the organizations participating to GSoC16 was published i started working on OpenKeychain.<br>\n<em>Some of my PRs are already merged</em> and during these weeks i’ve explored a large part of the codebase.<br>\nI’m familiar with the code of the UI and with that of the internal operations too, like you can see in those commits.</p>\n<p>As written in the complete proposal, i've an idea for a <strong>possible GSoC project</strong> (or as an preparatory work). But this is not a constraint. Working on other tasks would be equally great. In particular the first <strong>four projects</strong> listed on your page are pretty interesting. Also <strong>\"Detached Signatures\"</strong> would be good but i understand that maybe it's a bit too small for a complete GSoC. Maybe it can be good for the bonding period.</p>\n<p>All the other details are present in the complete proposal. Thank you.</p>\n<p>I hope to spend the summer on OpenKeychain with a <strong>GSoC 2016 project :)</strong></p>\n",
        "student_name": "runnerway",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/runnerway/137397da447fb796764bac37b57d835b",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/4985441539325952/"
      },
      {
        "title": "Move from Passwords to App Lock Mechanism",
        "short_description": "Migration to an App Lock Mechanism consists of 4 main tasks,\n1) Moving to usage of a single master password for all keys\n2) Adding encryption of the...",
        "description": "<p>Migration to an App Lock Mechanism consists of 4 main tasks,\n1) Moving to usage of a single master password for all keys\n2) Adding encryption of the entire database used for key storage\n3) Allowing a separate password for some keys (Optional) \n4) Adding an applock mechanism as added security</p>\n<p>Implementation of the above tasks gives added security to users, and also allows simplifying of the current codebase. Modifications to the existing database, adding of new user interfaces as well as refactoring of the codebase will be required in this task.</p>\n<p>A breakdown of the tasks involved along with proposed implementations for selected areas can be found in the full proposal.</p>\n",
        "student_name": "AlexFJW",
        "code_url": "https://gist.github.com/AlexFJW/0ddf4a10e7030ac991f8fb93af3decff",
        "project_url": "https://summerofcode.withgoogle.com/archive/2016/projects/5910458309541888/"
      }
    ]
  },
